---
// FRT-29: Terms of Service page. The service rules come from the legacy LA/TOS
// modal (index.html). Generic legal clauses use neutral wording ("the operators")
// because no legal entity, jurisdiction, or contact address is defined in the repo.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The rules for using the SPT Leaderboard: fair play, accounts, your content, moderation, and the limits of our responsibility."
>
  <article class="terms">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-11">October 11, 2026</time></p>

    <p>
      These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) apply to the SPT Leaderboard website (the “Service”).
      The Service is a public leaderboard for the SPT single-player mod. The mod tracks players,
      and the Service ranks them by score. Players can have public profiles, comments, friends, and teams.
      The SPT Leaderboard team runs the Service. In these Terms, “we,” “us,” and “the operators” mean that team.
    </p>
    <p>
      By submitting your statistics to the SPT Leaderboard, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree,
      do not use the Service. Violations can lead to removal from the leaderboard, profile bans, or permanent
      bans across all linked accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      You must be old enough to agree to these Terms where you live. By taking part in the leaderboard,
      you agree that you have read and understood these Terms. Missing a rule, or missing a recent update,
      does not excuse a violation.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair play</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Cheating and exploiting.</strong> Cheating, exploiting, and deception are not allowed. This includes
      changing key game data, such as PMC or SCAV level, quests, health, hydration, or energy. It also includes
      double armoring, which means wearing armor on top of other armor. For Ranked players, having a disallowed
      modification installed can count as a violation, at the discretion of the SPT Leaderboard team.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Allowed mods.</strong> Ranked players may use only cosmetic, weapon, AI, and quality-of-life (QoL)
      mods. Gameplay mods that give an unfair advantage are not allowed. Examples include, but are not limited to:
      god mode, unlimited ammo, faster reloads, extra loot, radars, post-death revival, debug mods, environment mods,
      and mods that loosen armor or headwear limits.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Casual Mode.</strong> In Casual Mode you may use gameplay-altering mods. You still may not exploit
      or harm the leaderboard. Casual Mode statistics do not count toward the main leaderboard rankings.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Data integrity.</strong> All submitted statistics must come from real gameplay. Sending falsified or
      edited data is a direct violation and leads to a permanent ban.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Your responsibility.</strong> Accounts sign in through the Network login. You are responsible for all
      activity under your profile and your secret token. Any submission or action made with your token counts as
      your action. Do not share your token or your account details.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Multiple accounts.</strong> You may link more than one account under the same token or identifier.
      If any linked account breaks these Terms, all linked accounts are held responsible. Penalties, including
      restrictions and bans, apply to the whole group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Account purpose.</strong> Accounts are for real player use only. Test accounts, developer accounts,
      and any account not used for legitimate gameplay are not allowed. A violation leads to a profile ban and
      removal from the leaderboard for that account. It can also apply to all linked accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Gameplay data and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>What the mod collects.</strong> When you install the client-side mod, it collects and sends gameplay
      data during active game sessions only. This includes, but is not limited to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>raid statistics, including location, coordinates, and player states</li>
      <li>inventory and gear</li>
      <li>profile progress, including skills, level, quests, and achievements</li>
      <li>Stattrack weapon statistics</li>
      <li>Fika Project configurations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The mod also reads and changes files in its own installation folder so that it can work.</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Stopping transmission.</strong> You can stop data from being sent at any time. Uninstall the mod,
      or disconnect the service from the F12 BepInEx menu.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Anonymous snapshots.</strong> A submitted dataset is an anonymous snapshot of one gameplay session in
      a modified environment. It is not personally identifiable information. Submitted datasets are not, and must
      not be, linked to real accounts, passwords, or email addresses.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>IP addresses.</strong> For anti-cheat analysis, a hashed or obfuscated version of your IP address may
      be collected with your token. The hashed IP is kept for no longer than one hour, then erased automatically.
      Only IP addresses flagged for malicious activity, such as brute-force attacks, are kept for developer review.
      Raw IP addresses are never logged.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> gives more detail about how we handle data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content and ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Your content means your username, profile picture, About Me text, comments, and replies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Ownership.</strong> You keep ownership of your content.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>License to us.</strong> You give the operators a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, store,
      copy, and display your content, and to format it, so the Service can work. The license for comments lasts
      while the comment is shown on the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Public leaderboard data.</strong> When you send data, you give the SPT Leaderboard a non-exclusive,
      royalty-free, perpetual license to use, display, and store your statistics publicly on the leaderboard and on
      related platforms. This covers all profile data sent to the server. Once submitted, data becomes part of the
      public leaderboard history. There is no technical process for deleting it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Removing comments.</strong> You can delete your own comments. Staff can remove any comment. A deleted
      comment may be hidden instead of erased.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your responsibility.</strong> You are responsible for what you post. Do not post content you have no
      right to share.
    </p>

    <h2>Content guidelines</h2>
    <p>
      All your content must suit a general audience. Content that is offensive, discriminatory, hateful, sexually
      explicit (NSFW), or politically charged is not allowed. This includes racism, sexual racism, religious
      intolerance, political extremism, hate speech, harassment, and any political discourse or propaganda.
    </p>
    <p>
      Breaking these rules can lead to removal from the leaderboard, a permanent restriction on profile changes,
      or a permanent ban.
    </p>

    <h2>Community features and rewards</h2>
    <p>
      Comments, friend requests and friend lists, and teams are part of the Service. The rules in these Terms
      apply to them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Battle-pass style cosmetic rewards, such as card backgrounds, borders, and icons, are earned through play.
      This site does not take payments or sell them, and they have no cash value.
    </p>

    <h2>Moderation and enforcement</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Automated flags.</strong> A profile flagged by an automated system for suspicious activity or abnormal
      statistics may receive a temporary ban while we investigate. You can appeal. Your appeal must include strong
      evidence that your profile is genuine. If you do not provide that evidence, the ban becomes permanent. You are
      responsible for keeping your profile within these Terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Moderation authority.</strong> The Administration and Moderation teams may review, change, or remove any
      entry without prior notice. All moderation decisions follow the principle of fair play. Decisions are final
      unless these Terms state an appeal option.
    </p>

    <h2>Service changes and availability</h2>
    <p>
      We may change the Service at any time. We may change season lengths, reset times, or scoring rules as needed.
      We may also change, pause, or stop the Service, in whole or in part, for a short time or for good. We can do
      this without notice and without liability.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
    <p>
      The Service relies on or links to third-party services. These include the Network login, Discord, GitHub, and
      the SPT mod’s pages. Those services follow their own terms and policies. We do not control them and are not
      responsible for them.
    </p>

    <h2>Warranties and disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind. This includes implied
      warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement, to the fullest extent
      permitted by law.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not guarantee that the Service will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free. We do not guarantee
      that rankings, statistics, or other results are accurate or complete.
    </p>
    <p>
      No internet service is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee the security of data you send. You use the
      Service at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, the SPT Leaderboard team, its developers, and its moderators are not
      liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages. This includes lost data,
      lost profits, and server interruptions, arising from your use of the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability to you for all claims related to the Service will
      not exceed the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim. The Service does not take payments,
      so this amount is normally zero.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some places do not allow certain limits. Where that applies, our liability is limited to the greatest extent
      the law allows.
    </p>

    <h2>Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to defend the operators and hold them harmless from claims, losses, costs, and reasonable legal fees.
      This applies to claims that arise from your use of the Service, your breach of these Terms, your content, or
      your violation of another person’s rights, including intellectual property rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>You can stop using the Service at any time.</p>
    <p>
      We can suspend or end your access at any time if you break these Terms, or if needed to protect the Service or
      other players.
    </p>
    <p>
      When access ends, your right to use the Service ends. The sections on ownership, public leaderboard data,
      warranties, liability, indemnification, and disputes stay in effect after that.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws in the place where the operators are based, without regard to
      conflict-of-law rules.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before starting a formal dispute, contact us and try to settle it first. Formal disputes go to the courts in
      that same place.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms do not remove any rights you have under the laws where you live that cannot be changed by contract.
    </p>

    <h2>General provisions</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Changes to these Terms.</strong> We may update these Terms at any time. We will change the “Last updated”
      date when we do. For material changes, we will post a notice on the Service. Continued use of the Service after
      an update means you accept the updated Terms. If you do not accept them, stop using the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Severability.</strong> If part of these Terms is found invalid, the rest still applies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Entire agreement.</strong> These Terms and the Privacy Policy are the full agreement between you and us
      about the Service. They replace earlier statements about the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>No waiver.</strong> If we do not enforce a rule right away, we do not give up the right to enforce it
      later.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Assignment.</strong> You may not transfer your account or your rights under these Terms. We may transfer
      these Terms to a successor that runs the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Force majeure.</strong> We are not responsible for delays or failures caused by events outside our
      reasonable control. Examples include natural disasters, power or internet outages, government actions, attacks,
      and failures of third-party services.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Notices.</strong> We may send notices by posting them on the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about these Terms, contact the SPT Leaderboard team through the Discord server or the project’s
      GitHub repository. Both links are in the footer.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Reading width for long-form prose. Spacing and type come from the shared tokens. */
  .terms {
    max-width: 46rem;
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .terms h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }
</style>
